<problem>
<!-- <title>discrete equilibria 7</title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="b" numToSelect="2" withReplacement="false" from="5" to="12" />
<selectFromSequence name="d" from="5" to="100" step="5" />
<select name="x">x y z u v w p X Y Z S</select>

<math name="answer" unordered="true">$b[1], $b[2]</math>

<math name="b_plus_c" simplify="full">$b[1] + $b[2]</math>
<math name="b_times_c" simplify="full">$b[1] $b[2]</math>

</setup>


<p>Find all equilibria to the discrete dynamical system below.  If there are multiple equilibria, separate your answers by commas.  
<md>
  <mrow>$x _{n+1}  - $x _n \amp= $x _n^2 - $b_plus_c $x _n + $b_times_c</mrow>
  <mrow>$x _0 \amp = $d</mrow>
</md>
</p>
<p><m>E =</m> 
<answer>
<award matchPartial="true" unorderedCompare="true">$answer </award>
</answer>
</p>


<solution>
<p>To find the equilibria, we set <m>$x _{n+1} = E</m> and <m>$x _n = E</m> in the evolution rule, obtaining
<md>
  <mrow>E-E\amp = E^2 - $b_plus_c E + $b_times_c</mrow>
  <mrow>0\amp = E^2 - $b_plus_c E + $b_times_c </mrow>
</md>
To factor the quadratic, we need to find factors of $b_times_c that add up to $b_plus_c .  The required factoring is <m>$b_times_c  = $b[1] \cdot $b[2] </m> as <m>$b[1] + $b[2]  = $b_plus_c </m>.  The quadratic factors as
<me>E^2 - $b_plus_c E + $b_times_c  = (E - $b[1] )(E - $b[2] ).</me> 
Since the quadratic must be zero, the equilibria are <m>E=$b[1] </m> and <m>E =$b[2] </m>.</p>


</solution>


</problem>